    "rich_text_UtJJmX": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "disabled": true,
      "settings": {
        "title": "What is a Stitch Count?",
        "heading_size": "heading-feature",
        "rich_text": "<p><strong>A stitch count refers to the total number of individual stitches used to create an embroidered design. It's a key factor in determining the complexity, size, and cost of an embroidery project. A higher stitch count often signifies a more intricate design or a larger design area, which may require more time and resources to complete. Stitch counts are vital for estimating thread usage, production time, and overall project cost. They also play a crucial role in selecting the right machine settings and ensuring the design fits perfectly on the chosen fabric or garment.</strong></p>",
        "display_on_card": true,
        "content_width_desktop": "lg:w-full",
